  "narrative": [
    {
      "text": "Figure C.4: \"Average Subsidy Progression for 1000 Agents\". The clearest of the three subsidy figures. Cyan (0.8), magenta (0.9) and red (0.7) all spike in the first few agents and are at zero within roughly 10, 10 and 40 agents; green (0.6) peaks near 0.075 and decays to zero by about agent 130; yellow (0.99) never leaves zero. Blue (0.51) again behaves differently in kind — it rises to about 0.022 by agent 100 and then decays very slowly, still paying about 0.011 at agent 1000. The error bars are dense enough to read as a band. Same qualitative story as Figure 6.3 at 100 agents, with the slow decay of the weakest-signal curve now visible over a longer horizon.",
      "state": "draft",
      "drafted_by": {
